there were some core aspects of that character&nbsp;
that I really felt connected to so much so that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:14.480
not just not just Sha-Risse but also people who&nbsp;
saw the film came up afterwards and they're like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:25.040
how how did you tell this story and it felt first&nbsp;
because because I sort of understood the pain of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:31.520
what that character was facing but but secondly&nbsp;
because I spent a lot of time understanding and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:38.480
being in that neighborhood and and I guess maybe&nbsp;
that is a bit of the documentarian side but&nbsp;&nbsp;

